<p class="sub-head">Temporary Point</p>
<p>When all <span lang="EN-US">values are set the new point will be visualised in the viewport as temporary entity. There are different types of temporary points:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>temporary construction point</b></span> - when a <span lang="EN-US">point</span> takes part in other entity definition, it appears in the viewport as temporary construction datum (white/black coloured by default). Its appearance can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Temporary Construction Datum</b></i></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>current construction point</b></span> - the currently edited/selected <span lang="EN-US">point</span> appears in the viewport as highlighted temporary datum (light red by default). Its colour can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Highlighted</b></i></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P2"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes</b></span>: If the temporary construction datum is currently edited, it appears as highlighted temporary datum.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>final construction point</b></span> - when all definition fields/all construction tabs are filled, then the <span lang="EN-US">point</span> appears in the viewport as final construction datum (green/black coloured by default). Its appearance can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Final Construction Datum.</b></i></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p3"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes</b></span>: If the current construction datum is actually the final one, then it will be coloured as final construction datum.</p>
<p>When this final construction datum is really created then its colour will be changed to the real datum colour (set in <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b><a href="../../References/Display_Settings-Colours.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours</a></b></i></span> ).</p>
